invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20.c guards its call to the vector path on a macro no build
  defines, so a CHACHA=vector object runs the portable loop under the
  vector name. Nothing else objects: chacha20_vector.c still compiles and
  links, bin/chacha20_equiv_test calls it directly, and every vector and
  Wycheproof case passes, because the portable loop computes the same
  bytes; only the time is wrong. CHACHA=vector is a statement about what
  the object runs, so the script compiles chacha20.c with
  -DCH_CHACHA_VECTOR and requires its object to call chacha20_vector_xor.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CHACHA_VECTOR
    // CHACHA=vector: the same keystream, four blocks at a time
--- new
#ifdef CH_CHACHA_VECTOR_PATH
    // CHACHA=vector: the same keystream, four blocks at a time
